latest_plan = "Based on the reflection, here's a detailed step-by-step plan to solve the challenge:\n\n1. Input Analysis:\n   a. Determine the dimensions of the input grid.\n   b. Identify if the pattern touches any edges of the input grid.\n   c. Extract the core pattern by removing surrounding black space.\n\n2. Output Grid Setup:\n   a. Calculate the output grid size: (2n-1) x (2n-1), where n is the larger dimension of the input grid.\n   b. Initialize the output grid with all black (0) cells.\n\n3. Pattern Scaling and Complexity:\n   a. Scale the core pattern to fit a quadrant of the output grid, maintaining its aspect ratio.\n   b. If the scaled pattern is too simple (covers less than 25% of a quadrant), enhance its complexity:\n      - Add surrounding cells to create a more intricate pattern.\n      - Ensure the enhanced pattern maintains the original pattern's characteristics.\n\n4. Pattern Placement:\n   a. Place the scaled and potentially enhanced pattern in the top-left quadrant.\n   b. Reflect and rotate the pattern to fill the other three quadrants:\n      - Top-right: reflect horizontally\n      - Bottom-left: reflect vertically\n      - Bottom-right: reflect both horizontally and vertically\n\n5. Central Void Creation:\n   a. Determine the void size based on the output grid dimensions:\n      - 1x1 for grids smaller than 11x11\n      - 3x3 for 11x11 to 13x13\n      - 5x5 for larger grids\n   b. Clear the central area to create the void.\n\n6. Edge Handling:\n   a. If the original input pattern touched any edge:\n      - Extend the pattern in the output grid to touch all edges.\n      - Fill any gaps along the edges with the most common adjacent non-black color.\n   b. If the original input didn't touch edges, but the output is smaller than 15x15:\n      - Extend a simplified version of the pattern to touch all edges.\n\n7. Symmetry Enforcement:\n   a. Iterate through the grid, ensuring perfect diagonal symmetry:\n      - For each cell (x, y), ensure (y, x) has the same value.\n   b. Repeat the process for the other diagonal.\n\n8. Final Adjustments:\n   a. Set the four corner cells of the output grid to black (0).\n   b. Perform a final pass to ensure no isolated black cells exist within the pattern:\n      - If a black cell is surrounded by non-black cells, fill it with the most common adjacent color.\n\n9. Validation:\n   a. Check that the output grid dimensions are correct.\n   b. Verify that the pattern has rotational symmetry.\n   c. Ensure the central void is present and of the correct size.\n   d. Confirm that the pattern touches all edges if required.\n\nThis plan addresses the key aspects of the challenge while incorporating the insights gained from the reflection. It provides a systematic approach to generate the required output, handling various input sizes and pattern complexities. The steps for enhancing simple patterns and handling edge cases should help in producing outputs that match the expected results across all test cases."
